The hudLayout folder manages HUD (heads-up display) settings that persist across sessions using localStorage, plus a runtime registry for the compact layout's plugin-fillable widget slots. It provides stores for layout mode preferences (classic vs. compact) and theme selection (default vs. slate-amber), enabling users to customize their HUD appearance, and hudWidgetRegistry.ts tracks which plugin currently owns each named slot (`hud.bottomStrip`, `hud.rightColumn`), broadcasting `shatteredarchive:hud-widget-updated` on every publish/clear. This folder integrates with the broader application by providing a centralized store for HUD preferences consumed by the MainContainer and settings UI, and (from Task 5/6 onward) the slot registry consumed by pluginHost.ts and the CompactWidgetSlot component.
